    "narrative": "For this June 11th slate, our offensive production hinges on mid-tier reliability rather than elite matchups, as we navigate a day with several key assets sidelined. **Geraldo Perdomo** stands as our strongest play with a 55.17 efficiency score; his favorable matchup against Phillips (4.33 xERA) and a prime spot in the #5 hole make him the most stable producer in today's lineup. **Taylor Ward** also earns a recommendation with a 52.92 score. While he faces the toughest arm of the day in Bryan Woo (3.42 xERA), the significant park-factor boost helps offset the SP-skill penalty, keeping him firmly in our starting outfield.\n\nThe remaining infield slots reflect the scarcity of high-upside options today. **Masyn Winn** (49.02) and **Gleyber Torres** (48.56) are marginal starts that offer floor-level value against average opposition. **Jeremiah Jackson** rounds out the starters at 45.63; while he benefits from a positive park shift, his projected #9 spot in the order suppresses his ceiling, making him a high-risk, high-reward play. It is a quiet day for the bench; with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Lawrence Butler** off, and **Cal Raleigh** continuing to navigate his IL stint, our rotation is constrained by availability rather than tough personnel choices. \n\nRegarding risks, the \"Lineup Pending\" status for both **Taylor Ward** and **Jeremiah Jackson** remains our primary concern; should they be dropped lower in their respective batting orders, their efficiency scores will likely dip below the 40-threshold, potentially threatening our game-cap efficiency. We are effectively playing a \"wait and see\" strategy with our fringe starters, trusting that the park factors for **Taylor Ward** and the lineup positioning for **Geraldo Perdomo** will provide the necessary base to hold steady in our 5x5 categories. Our rostered depth, including **Bryson Stott**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert**, remain on standby as we monitor potential late-scratches.",
